# File Size Limits

Keep **React components** and **functions** under **100 lines** each (from opening `{` to closing `}` of the declaration). Long units are harder to review, test, and reuse.

## What counts

- **Component** — the function body of `export function Foo()` or the memoized `FooComponent` before `memo()`
- **Function** — any named function, arrow export, server action, service method, or hook body
- **Do not count** — imports, types/interfaces at file top, or other exports in the same file

## When approaching the limit

Split before you hit 100 lines:

| Kind | Extract to |
| --- | --- |
| React UI sections | Colocated subcomponents in the same feature folder |
| Repeated JSX blocks | Named subcomponents (see [react-components](react-components.mdc)) |
| Component logic | Feature or shared hooks |
| Business steps | `services/`, `utils/`, or pure helpers — one export per file when possible |
| Server action steps | Private helpers in the same file or `services/` |

- ✅ Good:

  ```tsx
  function CheckoutSummary({ items }: Readonly<CheckoutSummaryProps>) {
    const subtotal = useCheckoutSubtotal(items)

    return (
      <section>
        <CheckoutLineItems items={items} />
        <CheckoutTotals subtotal={subtotal} />
      </section>
    )
  }
  ```

  ```typescript
  const validateCheckoutInput = (input: CheckoutInput) => { /* … */ }

  export const createCheckout = async (input: CheckoutInput) => {
    const validated = validateCheckoutInput(input)
    if (!validated) return null

    const session = await paymentGateway.createSession(validated)
    return session
  }
  ```

- ❌ Bad:

  ```tsx
  export function CheckoutPage() {
    // 150+ lines: form state, validation, fetch, error UI, and markup in one component
  }
  ```

  ```typescript
  export const handleWebhook = async (event: WebhookEvent) => {
    // 120 lines: verify, switch on type, DB updates, email, analytics — split by step
  }
  ```

## Exceptions

- **Test files** (`*.spec.ts`, `*.spec.tsx`, `__tests__/`) — no hard limit; still prefer focused describes and shared fixtures
- **Config/data tables** — large static maps are fine if mostly literal entries; move lookup logic to helpers when behavior grows

